---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHOR } from '../../lib/site.mjs';
---
<Page title="Contact & Report a Data Error | CarSpecFix" description="Contact CarSpecFix, report a wrong figure on any page, or ask for a vehicle to be added — what to include and how long a reply takes." path="/contact/" crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Contact', url: '/contact/' }]} h1="Contact">
<p>Every page on this site ends with a box you can write in, and it reaches the same inbox as <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Both are read by <a href={`/authors/${AUTHOR.slug}/`}>{AUTHOR.name}</a>. Use whichever is closer to hand.</p>
<p>The form below is the one to use for a <em>wrong figure</em>: it asks for the page, the value and the source you are checking against, which is exactly what a correction needs. A general question — a car we do not cover yet, a code that has no page — belongs in the box at the bottom of any page.</p>
<p>There is no support desk and no ticket number: replies come from one person, usually within a few working days. A report with the page and the source you are checking against gets fixed fastest — a report that says only "this is wrong" usually needs a second email before anything can change.</p>

<h2 class="section__title" id="report-form">Report a data error</h2>
<form class="feedback" data-report style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;max-width:560px">
  <input class="hp-field" type="text" name="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true">
  <label class="field"><span>Page</span><input name="page" required placeholder="/specs/honda/civic/2022/"></label>
  <label class="field"><span>Which value? (e.g. oil capacity, front psi)</span><input name="field" required maxlength="200"></label>
  <label class="field"><span>What's wrong, and the source you're checking against (no personal info)</span><textarea name="details" required maxlength="2000"></textarea></label>
  <div><button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send report</button></div>
  <p role="status" class="feedback__msg"></p>
</form>
<script is:inline>(function(){var p=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('report');var f=document.querySelector('[data-report]');if(p&&f&&/^\/[a-z0-9\/-]*$/.test(p))f.page.value=p})();</script>

<h2 class="section__title">What makes a report actionable</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The page URL</strong> — the full path, for example <code>/specs/toyota/rav4/2024/</code>. Vehicle year and model in the text is enough if the URL is not to hand.</li>
<li><strong>Which figure</strong> — "oil capacity", "front tyre pressure", "the recall count". One report per figure is easier to track than a list.</li>
<li><strong>The source you are reading</strong> — the manual, the page number, or the NHTSA campaign number. If your number comes from a different model year or a different market's manual, that is worth saying: it is the single most common reason two figures disagree.</li>
<li><strong>No personal information.</strong> The form asks for none and none is stored. Do not paste a VIN, an address or a phone number.</li>
</ul>
<p>What happens next: the report is checked against the cited document. If the page is wrong, the figure is corrected, the page gets a new verification date, and it reappears on the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>. If the page is right and the discrepancy comes from a different model year or edition, the reply will say which document the published figure came from.</p>

<h2 class="section__title">Other reasons to write</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Request a vehicle.</strong> Coverage grows by verified vehicle, so requests are useful. Model year, engine and trim narrow it down; a request for "all Camrys" cannot be answered without one.</li>
<li><strong>Request a trouble code or symptom.</strong> Say what the car did and, if you have it, the code the reader showed.</li>
<li><strong>Copyright or image enquiries.</strong> See the <a href="/copyright/">copyright page</a> for how images are licensed and how to ask for a removal.</li>
<li><strong>Privacy and data requests.</strong> See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what is held and how to ask for it.</li>
</ul>
</Page>
